>> Random numbers

  rand(lo, hi)
      A random int in [lo, hi] inclusive (raises if lo > hi).
  randf(lo, hi)
      A random float in [lo, hi] (raises if lo > hi or not finite).
>> Slices (copy-on-write)

var s = a[1:3];

A slice is a cheap VIEW until written: reading it shares the parent's storage, and a write clones first so logically-distinct arrays never bleed into each other. intptr(x) reveals when two values share storage.
>> Exceptions

  Exceptions  [trycatch]
